# Repo-root tooling and docs that the installed extension never reads. Keeps the
# bundle to what Claude Desktop runs: manifest, icon, server/, node_modules/,
# package.json, LICENSE. (mcpb's built-in defaults already drop .git,
# package-lock.json, *.mcpb and the like.)
# Leading "/" anchors each entry to the repo root; unanchored, README.md and
# scripts/ would also strip files inside node_modules/ packages.
/.github/
/scripts/
/glama.json
/README.md

# Python bytecode from running scripts/ locally. scripts/ is already excluded
# above; these keep a stray __pycache__ anywhere else out of the bundle.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
